A||||11||Steven||G-Tech Pro||||5||
Z||000000||Steven||06-27-2001||05:42 PM||||The G-Tech Pro show hp at the wheel. How much hp do you generally lose thur the drive train?<P>------------------<BR>85 Fiero GT<BR>3.2 liter w/4sp manual trans<BR>Silver.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Greg Piet||06-27-2001||07:58 PM||||15% is a number I hear a lot for drivetrain loss.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||06-27-2001||10:46 PM||||How do you like your G-Tech?  I have been thinking of getting one for quite a while now...<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steven||06-28-2001||09:28 AM||||Well it is really belongs to a friend of mine. He let me use it earlier in the week, and again over this weekend. It was very easy to work, but I don't know how useful of an everyday thing it is. If you buy one, I think you would use it for about 3-5 days, then maybe not again untill you do some tuning, or start having what might be the beginning of a performance problem. It might be better just to use a friends, unless you "must have one".||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||06-28-2001||12:10 PM||||I have one & I like it. I think is a very good tool for the price. My problem is that here are so many cops (or people who call them) that is hard for me to find empty streets near to do the thing. When you do hard launches and the engine is screaming everybody looks :-(||||reg||1
Z||000005||speed racer||06-28-2001||12:26 PM||||alex how do accurate is it ||||reg||1
Z||000006||90ZR1||06-28-2001||12:31 PM||||I have not used one yet, but BFGoodrich has a deal going on wright now if you buy 4 tires you get one for free.  It is listed on there website.  So I am going to be getting one.  There address is <A HREF="http://www.bfgoodrichtires.com." TARGET=_blank>www.bfgoodrichtires.com.</A> <P>------------------<BR>Greg Kitt<BR>90 Red/Red Zr-1<BR>88 Fiero GT White/Gray||||reg||10
Z||000007||1FST2M6||06-28-2001||02:30 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.dynojet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dynojet.com</A>  don't waste your $ on a g-tech. get more accurate repeatable results off an inertia dyno. <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||06-28-2001||03:43 PM||||Well.. for the price of my G-tech I can only get one & a quater dyno session here ($100!). Even at $50 you can do only three. With the G-tech you have more flexibility. I know the dyno will give you HP & torque but what you really want to know after your mods is if you are faster. G-Techs are very accurate. I browse a Vette forum and many people there have it and say its not more than 0.2s off of the track times. I clocked my auto C5 Vette to 5.3s 0-60. That's what the magazines advertise for it (couple ticks slower than the stick).<P>------------------<BR>Alex4mula<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.zing.com/picture/p69fbfe3e99ec5a0b81c10afcc578ff95/fe6d5c42.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Black88GT||06-28-2001||05:04 PM||||I agree with Alex4mula, the closest dyno is an hours drive away and it costs like 150 dollars an hour.  The Gtec can be used anytime you want and its a one time fee.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Greg Piet||06-28-2001||05:33 PM||||The Gtech is OK...<BR>I use it for skidpad and autox lateral g's primarily...<P>The biggest problem I have with it is finding a nice flat straight piece of road that I can use to properly measure the 0-60-0 or 1/4 or hp.  I wouldnt expect it to be as good as a dyno test(you get what you pay for), but it gives you a good ballpark figure.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||TRiAD||06-28-2001||07:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B> <A HREF="http://www.dynojet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dynojet.com</A>  don't waste your $ on a g-tech. get more accurate repeatable results off an inertia dyno. <P>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-28-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That may be true for HP, I've only ever used mine for Gs and accelleration. It is <I>completely</I> reliable, accurate and repeatable for those. <P><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
